{% comment %}
  THE DURABLE HALF OF THE BANK PAYMENT INSTRUCTIONS (register D12).

  Reads `GET /apps/carat/bank-payment-orders`
  (app/app/routes/apps.carat.bank-payment-orders.tsx) through
  `assets/bank-payment-orders.js` and renders the signed-in customer's own
  Bank Payment orders -- Buy Now and Group Buy -- with full payment
  instructions for the ones still awaiting money.

  WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS. Payment instructions used to reach the customer
  through exactly one channel, an email. An email-provider outage therefore
  produced a customer holding a real order with no idea where to send funds.
  The checkout confirmation panel covers the moment of checkout; this page
  covers every moment after it -- a bookmarkable place the customer can
  return to, days later, on a different device.

  AUTHORIZATION IS SERVER-SIDE AND IS NOT THIS FILE'S JOB. The Liquid
  `customer` branch below is a COURTESY ONLY: it avoids showing a signed-out
  shopper a panel that can only ever fail. It is not a security control and
  must never be treated as one. The route authorizes on
  `logged_in_customer_id` from the SIGNED App Proxy parameters, matched
  exactly against the order's stored `customerGid`. Nothing this template or
  its JS sends -- no email, no order id, no customer id -- participates in
  that decision, and the fetch below deliberately passes no identity
  parameter at all. Same pattern and same reasoning as
  `sections/warranty-claim-form.liquid`'s signed-out branch.

  NO COORDINATES ARE EVER BAKED INTO THIS TEMPLATE. Zelle recipient, bank
  name, routing and account numbers arrive per request in the JSON response
  and are written with `textContent` by the JS. They are never rendered by
  Liquid, never cached, and never stored (`paymentInstructionsView.ts`: "THIS
  OBJECT IS NEVER PERSISTED. NOT ANYWHERE."). A theme file is a public,
  cacheable asset; a payment destination does not belong in one.

  COPY STATUS. The sign-in gate sentence carries the exact owner-approved
  sentence from `docs/REQUIRED-CUSTOMER-ACCOUNTS.md` section 4 ("Please sign
  in or create a CaratForUs account to continue."), pinned in
  `app/app/theme/ownerApprovedCopy.test.ts` alongside the identical sentence
  in `snippets/bank-payment-checkout-dialog.liquid` and
  `sections/warranty-claim-form.liquid`. The commitment notice, the
  still-required sentence and the include-with-payment sentence are NOT in
  this file's locale keys at all -- they are composed server-side by
  `buildPaymentInstructionsView` so that one approved wording serves the
  confirmation panel, this page and the email. Every other string here is
  draft labelling copy, same status as the rest of this theme's
  `bank_payment_checkout_form.*` keys.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'component-bank-payment-orders.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div class="color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} isolate gradient">
  <div
    class="carat-bank-orders section-{{ section.id }}-padding page-width"
    data-carat-bank-orders-section
  >
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="carat-bank-orders__heading {{ section.settings.heading_size }}">
        {{ section.settings.heading | escape }}
      </h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if customer -%}
      <p class="carat-bank-orders__intro">
        {{- 'templates.bank_payment_orders.intro' | t -}}
      </p>

      {%- comment -%}
        The JS replaces this region entirely. Until it does, the customer sees
        a loading line rather than an empty page -- and if the script fails to
        load at all, the noscript fallback below still names where to ask.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div
        class="carat-bank-orders__results"
        data-carat-bank-orders-results
        role="status"
        aria-live="polite"
        aria-busy="true"
      >
        <p class="carat-bank-orders__loading" data-carat-bank-orders-loading>
          {{- 'templates.bank_payment_orders.loading' | t -}}
        </p>
      </div>

      <noscript>
        <p class="carat-bank-orders__noscript">
          {{- 'templates.bank_payment_orders.noscript' | t -}}
        </p>
      </noscript>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Signed out. Courtesy branch -- see this section's header comment.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="carat-bank-orders__signin-required" data-carat-bank-orders-signin-required>
        <h3 class="carat-bank-orders__signin-heading">
          {{- 'templates.bank_payment_orders.sign_in_required_heading' | t -}}
        </h3>
        <p class="carat-bank-orders__signin-message">
          {{- 'templates.bank_payment_orders.sign_in_required_message' | t -}}
        </p>
        <div class="carat-bank-orders__actions">
          <a
            href="{{ routes.account_login_url }}?return_url={{ request.path | url_encode }}"
            class="button"
            data-carat-bank-orders-signin-link
          >
            {{- 'customer.log_in' | t -}}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

<script src="{{ 'bank-payment-orders.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% style %}
  .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom | times: 0.75 | round: 0 }}px;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .section-{{ section.id }}-padding {
      padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Bank Payment orders",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "heading_size",
      "options": [
        { "value": "h2", "label": "Small" },
        { "value": "h1", "label": "Medium" },
        { "value": "h0", "label": "Large" }
      ],
      "default": "h1",
      "label": "Heading size"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Section padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Top padding",
      "default": 36
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Bottom padding",
      "default": 36
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Bank Payment orders"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
